      "Each phrase carries a plain wish. Saha means together, nau means both of us, and avatu means may he protect, so the opening asks the divine to protect teacher and student jointly. Bhunaktu is may he nourish or sustain. Viryam is vigour or strength, and karavavahai is let us two act, so the third line asks for energy in shared work. Tejasvi is radiant or keen, adhitam is what has been studied, and astu is let it be. The final line, ma vidvishavahai, means may we not hate or quarrel with each other.",
